      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "Great question! D\u00e9j\u00e0 vu is one of the brain's most fascinating and mysterious phenomena. Here's a breakdown of what we know:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83e\udde0 What Is D\u00e9j\u00e0 Vu?\n\n",
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "citations": [
          {
            "cited_text": "Studies of epileptic patients investigated via intracerebral electrodes demonstrate that stimulation of the rhinal cortex (such ...\n\nD\u00e9j\u00e0 vu is a Fren...",
            "encrypted_index": "Eo8BCioIEBgCIiRkMmJjZWZjOS0wNDQwLTQxYWUtOTM0Mi1hNDFhNjdkYWIzZWQSDAVOXADp+eKcbRRQIRoMT7+7Mj0QpzvkbyDZIjBa9gyNmtG9iN8OuRkB4p+0A7ePsfCAICCewsjwqUyII8KRcMvC3SkB3Hb975XII+UqE9g0p0y6gkE9nl4Z2cBuy1BRr/sYBA==",
            "title": "The Neuroscience of D\u00e9j\u00e0 Vu | Psychology Today",
            "type": "web_search_result_location",
            "url": "https://www.psychologytoday.com/us/blog/brain-babble/201208/the-neuroscience-d-j-vu"
          }
        ],
        "text": "D\u00e9j\u00e0 vu is a French term that literally means \"already seen\" and is reported to occur in 60\u201370% of people, most commonly between the ages of 15 and 25.",
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": " ",
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "citations": [
          {
            "cited_text": "Most of the theories share a similar idea, that d\u00e9j\u00e0 vu happens when parts of the brain tell us that a past experience is repeating itself.\n\n",
            "encrypted_index": "Eo8BCioIEBgCIiRkMmJjZWZjOS0wNDQwLTQxYWUtOTM0Mi1hNDFhNjdkYWIzZWQSDHCQX/kf9LLWkiLhhRoMPkTCpVRTIGhShTykIjB/4mSmQFY6EXhz04EKtkFF1tYMhK+wSOYD9Prr9eFhcWp4/j2lIwbRZzFLzXVo7p4qE7j64Rh5P9Rnj7l2FyhWMOdzykcYBA==",
            "title": "D\u00e9j\u00e0 Vu: The neuroscience behind the mysterious phenomenon",
            "type": "web_search_result_location",
            "url": "https://www.inspirethemind.org/post/d%C3%A9j%C3%A0-vu-the-neuroscience-behind-the-mysterious-phenomenon"
          }
        ],
        "text": "Most theories share a similar idea: that d\u00e9j\u00e0 vu happens when parts of the brain tell us that a past experience is repeating itself.",
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd2c What's Happening in the Brain?\n\nAt its core, ",
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "citations": [
          {
            "cited_text": "\u201cD\u00e9j\u00e0 vu is caused by dysfunctional connections between the parts of your brain that play a role in memory recollection and familiarity,\u201d Dr. Khoury e...",
            "encrypted_index": "EpEBCioIEBgCIiRkMmJjZWZjOS0wNDQwLTQxYWUtOTM0Mi1hNDFhNjdkYWIzZWQSDFZIXvbL0Ch/W1hrAhoMGqcNiFhwWQ/ga80qIjAqU94vyk94gBSyFO4w3b4DdxcZy2GvsWRgjz16gc0PsmEd90Sl4XD3s3k8vtf6MLoqFdeMTb4qTLh14YS0crlpPBOkNZ+RyxgE",
            "title": "D\u00e9j\u00e0 Vu: What It Is and Why It Happens",
            "type": "web_search_result_location",
            "url": "https://health.clevelandclinic.org/deja-vu-what-it-is-and-when-it-may-be-cause-for-concern"
          }
        ],
        "text": "\"d\u00e9j\u00e0 vu is caused by dysfunctional connections between the parts of your brain that play a role in memory recollection and familiarity.\" It's \"a misfire that blurs the line between memory and new experience.\"",
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "\n\nMore specifically, ",
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "citations": [
          {
            "cited_text": "\u201cIt\u2019s a misfire that blurs the line between memory and new experience.\u201d \u00b7 In other words, it happens when there\u2019s a miscommunication between two parts...",
            "encrypted_index": "EpABCioIEBgCIiRkMmJjZWZjOS0wNDQwLTQxYWUtOTM0Mi1hNDFhNjdkYWIzZWQSDOsbiyW7L+oiSzFNEBoMs/74vnFqGNVI9lauIjCfTZBtBmPcqKrHbd1fthtWqwtCc06p1tB9RAvX5AniewtbeuSx9OX9GzpQlkkL4roqFE2cPKBlO0HyGdGl11O8Z1rUSfiqGAQ=",
            "title": "D\u00e9j\u00e0 Vu: What It Is and Why It Happens",
            "type": "web_search_result_location",
            "url": "https://health.clevelandclinic.org/deja-vu-what-it-is-and-when-it-may-be-cause-for-concern"
          }
        ],
        "text": "it happens when there's a miscommunication between two parts of your brain: the one responsible for memories (your temporal lobe) and the one responsible for taking in new information (your hippocampus).",
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "\n\n",
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "citations": [
          {
            "cited_text": "Scientists suggest that, at least in epilepsy, d\u00e9j\u00e0 vu episodes may arise from seizures in the brain's temporal lobe or dysfunction in brain regions i...",
            "encrypted_index": "Eo8BCioIEBgCIiRkMmJjZWZjOS0wNDQwLTQxYWUtOTM0Mi1hNDFhNjdkYWIzZWQSDBYh3MQTUuVcWhNy9RoMyR+3WwO3UiC0gkE0IjBq+EkNRYADFXECmAaKdnfWwBzp1r8A9/SOyfVEVTWlOg2w3QUtXCQ9ta2hW6bc+d0qE9H/wwit/0N63QLe5KJOsLS3znsYBA==",
            "title": "What is the science behind d\u00e9j\u00e0 vu? | Live Science",
